 537:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			/** Stalls the current endpoint, indicating to the host that a logical problem occurred with the
 538:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  indicated endpoint and that the current transfer sequence should be aborted. This provides a
 539:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  way for devices to indicate invalid commands to the host so that the current transfer can be
 540:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  aborted and the host can begin its own recovery sequence.
 541:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *
 542:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  The currently selected endpoint remains stalled until either the \ref Endpoint_ClearStall() 
 543:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  is called, or the host issues a CLEAR FEATURE request to the device for the currently select
 544:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *  endpoint.
 545:../lufa-LUFA-111009/LUFA/Drivers/USB/Core/AVR8/../AVR8/../AVR8/Endpoint_AVR8.h **** 			 *
